{"annotations": [], "blocks": [{"bbox": [49.585999999999956, 73.755, 120.32799999999995, 80.18099999999993], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "caption", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 9, "seq": 0, "source": "docling", "text": "TABLE 3 (Continued)"}, {"bbox": [49.57649999999995, 522.4694999999999, 545.2305000000001, 572.8251450068399], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 9, "seq": 1, "source": "docling", "text": "AF, angina frequency; AS, angina stability; CCS, Canadian Cardiovascular Society; CI, confidence interval; DP, disease perception; EQ-5D-5L, EuroQol-5-Dimensions-5-Level; FAS, full analysis set; NA, not applicable; PL, physical limitation; PPS, per-protocol analysis set; PSQI, Pittsburgh sleep quality index; QBS, Qi stagnation and Blood stasis; SAQ, Seattle Angina Questionnaire; TS, treatment satisfaction; VAS, visual analog scale; XZOL, Xuefu Zhuyu oral liquid; Zung-SAS, Zung Self-rating Anxiety Scale; Zung-SDS, Zung Self-rating Depression Scale. a Statistical significance was calculated based on data distribution. Pvalues were calculated with a Mann-Whitney U -test between the 2 groups for angina attack frequency; angina attack duration; use of rescue medicine and CCS grading for eort angina. Pvalues for SAQ; EQ-5D-5L index; EQ-5D-5L VAS and PSQI were calculated with an independent-samples t -test between the 2 groups. Pvalues for Qi stagnation and Blood stasis pattern changes were calculated with a chi-square test."}, {"bbox": [49.586, 584.25, 185.74299999999997, 590.6759999999999], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "caption", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 9, "seq": 2, "source": "docling", "text": "TABLE 4 Adverse events for both groups."}, {"bbox": [49.586, 771.72286, 351.467, 778.6224286694102], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 9, "seq": 3, "source": "docling", "text": "AEs,